ngm:video-streaming a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Video Streaming"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Video Streaming is the continuous, real-time transmission of encoded video data over a network to a client that decodes and renders the content progressively, without requiring the full file to be downloaded first. In metaverse and virtual production contexts it encompasses live streaming, adaptive bitrate (ABR) delivery, 360-degree video, and volumetric video streaming, each with distinct latency, bandwidth, and codec requirements."@en ;
