ngm:european-commission a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "European Commission"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The European Commission is the politically independent executive body of the European Union responsible for proposing legislation, implementing Council decisions, managing the EU budget, and upholding EU treaties and law across all member states. In the technology domain, it has initiated and co-authored major regulatory frameworks including the AI Act, the Data Governance Act, the Digital Markets Act, and the Digital Services Act, collectively constituting a comprehensive digital regulatory agenda. It also funds research through programmes such as Horizon Europe and coordinates AI standardisation mandates issued to CEN-CENELEC and ETSI."@en ;
