ngm:cryptographic-security a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Cryptographic Security"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Cryptographic Security is the application of cryptographic primitives and protocols—including symmetric and asymmetric encryption, digital signatures, hash functions, and zero-knowledge proofs—to protect data confidentiality, integrity, and authenticity. In blockchain and metaverse contexts it underpins transaction authorisation, identity verification, secure key management, and privacy-preserving computation, forming the bedrock upon which trustless systems and decentralised applications are built."@en ;
